  "evidence": "Original N/E/U shows a sustained negative shift starting near index 485 (P1 onset), with values dropping ~3–6 mm in N/E/U and remaining offset through index 509. A clear opposing return is not observed: after index 509, values remain low (e.g., indices 510–517 stay near -5 to -6 mm in N/E), and the small positive offsets for P2/P3 are inconsistent with a coherent return—P2’s tiny offsets (~0.4 mm) lack physical coherence across axes, and P3 is a single-point spike (index 514) that aligns with a local noise/step, not a platform. The numerical tool’s best pulse candidate (514–515) is rejected and coincides with missing data at 519–522, further undermining P2/P3 as genuine temporary platforms. No sustained return across same axes supports P1 as a complete temporary offset; instead, the drop appears permanent or part of longer-term motion. Thus, no genuine temporary platform exists in this interval.",
